content.explanation:
**Taking Your Setup Further:**

Karate offers extensive customization options to adapt the framework to your specific needs—from environment configuration to custom logging and integration with other tools.

**1. karate-config.js - Environment Configuration**

The main configuration file that runs before any tests:

```javascript
// karate-config.js
function fn() {
    var env = karate.env || 'dev';

    var config = {
        env: env,
        baseUrl: 'https://' + env + '-api.example.com',
        timeout: 10000
    };

    if (env == 'dev') {
        config.authToken = 'dev-token';
        config.timeout = 15000;
    } else if (env == 'prod') {
        config.authToken = karate.properties['auth.token'];
        config.timeout = 5000;
    }

    // Configure HTTP settings
    karate.configure('connectTimeout', 5000);
    karate.configure('readTimeout', config.timeout);
    karate.configure('ssl', true);

    return config;
}
```

**2. Environment-Specific Config Files**

Karate automatically loads environment-specific configuration:

```
src/test/resources/
├── karate-config.js              # Default (loaded first)
├── karate-config-dev.js          # Loaded when env=dev
├── karate-config-staging.js      # Loaded when env=staging
└── karate-config-prod.js         # Loaded when env=prod
```

**Example karate-config-dev.js:**

```javascript
function fn() {
    var config = {
        baseUrl: 'https://dev-api.example.com',
        dbUrl: 'jdbc:mysql://dev-db:3306/test',
        timeout: 15000
    };
    return config;
}
```

**3. Tagging for Selective Execution**

Organize tests with tags for targeted execution:

```gherkin
@smoke
Scenario: Critical login test
    * url baseUrl
    * path '/login'
    * request { username: 'admin', password: 'admin' }
    * method post
    * status 200

@regression
Scenario: Comprehensive user test
    # ... longer test

@performance @slow
Scenario: Load test
    # ... performance test

@ignore
Scenario: Work in progress
    # ... not ready yet
```

```bash
# Run only smoke tests
mvn test -Dkarate.options="--tags @smoke"

# Run regression and performance, exclude smoke
mvn test -Dkarate.options="--tags @regression,@performance --tags ~@smoke"

# Run all except ignored
mvn test -Dkarate.options="--tags ~@ignore"
```

**4. Custom Headers and SSL**

Configure global headers and SSL settings:

```javascript
// In karate-config.js
karate.configure('headers', {
    'Accept': 'application/json',
    'User-Agent': 'Karate-Test',
    'X-API-Key': config.apiKey
});

// Disable SSL verification (for testing only - use with caution!)
karate.configure('ssl', true);

// Custom trust store for corporate environments
karate.configure('ssl', {
    keyStore: 'classpath:keystore.jks',
    keyStorePassword: 'changeit',
    trustStore: 'classpath:truststore.jks',
    trustStorePassword: 'changeit'
});
```

**5. Custom Logging**

Control what gets logged:

```javascript
// Configure log levels
karate.configure('logPrettyRequest', true);   // Pretty print JSON requests
karate.configure('logPrettyResponse', true);  // Pretty print JSON responses
karate.configure('showLog', true);            // Show log messages

// Custom logger
var Logger = Java.type('java.util.logging.Logger');
var logger = Logger.getLogger('karate');
logger.info('Custom log message');

// Conditional logging
* def debug = karate.env == 'dev' ? true : false
* if (debug) karate.log('Request payload:', request)
```

**6. Report Customization**

Customize test reports:

```xml
<!-- Maven surefire plugin configuration -->
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
    <version>3.0.0-M7</version>
    <configuration>
        <systemPropertyVariables>
            <karate.env>${karate.env}</karate.env>
            <karate.options>${karate.options}</karate.options>
        </systemPropertyVariables>
        <reportNameSuffix>karate-tests-${karate.env}</reportNameSuffix>
    </configuration>
</plugin>
```

```javascript
// In karate-config.js - customize report output
karate.configure('report', {
    showLog: true,
    showAllSteps: false,
    timestamp: true
});
```

**7. Parallel Execution Configuration**

Fine-tune parallel test execution:

```xml
<!-- Maven Karate plugin with parallel configuration -->
<plugin>
    <groupId>com.intuit.karate</groupId>
    <artifactId>karate-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <version>${karate.version}</version>
    <executions>
        <execution>
            <phase>test</phase>
            <goals>
                <goal>test</goal>
            </goals>
            <configuration>
                <parallel>4</parallel>           <!-- Number of parallel threads -->
                <threads>4</threads>             <!-- Thread pool size -->
                <parallelTests>all</parallelTests><!-- Which tests to run in parallel -->
                <failIfNoTests>true</failIfNoTests>
                <tags>~@ignore</tags>            <!-- Exclude ignored tests -->
            </configuration>
        </execution>
    </executions>
</plugin>
```

**8. Integration with Other Frameworks**

Integrate Karate with Spring Boot:

```java
// Spring Boot integration
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import com.intuit.karate.junit5.Karate;

@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = SpringBootTest.WebEnvironment.DEFINED_PORT)
class SpringKarateTest {

    @Karate.Test
    Karate testApi() {
        // Spring context will be available during test execution
        return Karate.run("api-test").relativeTo(getClass());
    }
}
```

Integrate with TestContainers:

```java
@Testcontainers
class ContainerKarateTest {

    @Container
    static GenericContainer<?> redis = new GenericContainer<>("redis:6-alpine")
        .withExposedPorts(6379);

    @Karate.Test
    Karate testWithRedis() {
        System.setProperty("redis.port", redis.getFirstMappedPort().toString());
        return Karate.run().relativeTo(getClass());
    }
}
```

**9. Custom Function Libraries**

Create reusable JavaScript utilities:

```javascript
// utils.js
function getRandomEmail() {
    var timestamp = new Date().getTime();
    return 'user' + timestamp + '@test.com';
}

function formatDate(date) {
    var year = date.getFullYear();
    var month = (date.getMonth() + 1).toString().padStart(2, '0');
    var day = date.getDate().toString().padStart(2, '0');
    return year + '-' + month + '-' + day;
}

function calculateTotal(price, quantity, tax) {
    return price * quantity * (1 + tax);
}

function generateUser() {
    var id = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000);
    return {
        id: id,
        username: 'user_' + id,
        email: 'user_' + id + '@test.com'
    };
}
```

```gherkin
* def utils = call read('classpath:utils.js')
* def email = utils.getRandomEmail()
* def today = utils.formatDate(new Date())
* def total = utils.calculateTotal(100, 2, 0.1)
* def user = utils.generateUser()
```

**10. Configuration Properties**

Load configuration from properties files:

```properties
# config.properties
api.base.url=https://api.example.com
api.timeout=10000
api.retry.count=3
db.user=testuser
db.password=testpass
```

```javascript
// karate-config.js
var java = Java.type('java.util.Properties');
var props = new java();
props.load(new java.io.FileInputStream('config.properties'));

var config = {
    baseUrl: props.getProperty('api.base.url'),
    timeout: parseInt(props.getProperty('api.timeout')),
    retryCount: parseInt(props.getProperty('api.retry.count'))
};

// Use in tests
* print 'Using baseUrl:', baseUrl
```

**11. Advanced Maven Configuration**

Use Maven profiles for different environments:

```xml
<profiles>
    <profile>
        <id>dev</id>
        <properties>
            <karate.env>dev</karate.env>
            <skip.tests>false</skip.tests>
        </properties>
    </profile>
    <profile>
        <id>prod</id>
        <properties>
            <karate.env>prod</karate.env>
            <skip.tests>false</skip.tests>
        </properties>
    </profile>
    <profile>
        <id>skip-tests</id>
        <properties>
            <skip.tests>true</skip.tests>
        </properties>
    </profile>
</profiles>
```

```bash
# Run with dev profile
mvn test -Pdev

# Run with prod profile
mvn test -Pprod

# Skip tests
mvn install -Pskip-tests
```

**12. Configuration Options Summary**

| Option | Description | Example |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `karate.env` | Environment name | `-Dkarate.env=dev` |
| `karate.options` | Karate CLI options | `-Dkarate.options="--tags @smoke"` |
| `karate.config.dir` | Config directory | `-Dkarate.config.dir=/path/to/config` |
| `karate.output.dir` | Output directory | `-Dkarate.output.dir=/path/to/output` |
| `karate.port` | Mock server port | `-Dkarate.port=8080` |
| `karate.ssl` | SSL configuration | `-Dkarate.ssl=true` |
| `karate.debug` | Enable debug mode | `-Dkarate.debug=true` |
| `karate.width` | Console width | `-Dkarate.width=120` |

**13. Programmatic Configuration**

Configure Karate programmatically in Java:

```java
import com.intuit.karate.Runner;
import java.util.Collections;

public class CustomRunner {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Runner.path("classpath:com/example/users.feature")
            .tags("@smoke")
            .parallel(4)
            .reportDir("target/custom-reports")
            .karateEnv("staging")
            .systemProperty("user", "test")
            .hook(new CustomHook())
            .run();
    }
}
```

**14. Troubleshooting Advanced Setup**

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| **Configuration not loading** | Check karate-config.js is in src/test/resources |
| **Environment not detected** | Pass -Dkarate.env explicitly or check spelling |
| **Tags not working** | Ensure tag syntax (@tag) and spacing correct |
| **Parallel execution too slow** | Reduce thread count, check for shared resources |
| **SSL errors** | Configure truststore or set karate.configure('ssl', true) |
| **Report generation fails** | Check write permissions on target directory |
| **Custom headers not applied** | Headers configured in background or karate-config.js |
| **JavaScript functions not found** | Check path in read() statement |
| **Properties file not loading** | Use absolute path or classpath: prefix |
| **Maven profile not activating** | Check profile syntax and activation conditions |

**15. Best Practices for Configuration**

✅ **Use environment-specific config** – Separate dev, staging, prod settings
✅ **Keep secrets out of version control** – Use environment variables or secure vaults
✅ **Tag tests meaningfully** – @smoke, @regression, @performance for targeted runs
✅ **Configure logging appropriately** – Debug in dev, minimal in prod
✅ **Use custom functions for reuse** – Centralize common logic in utility files
✅ **Document configuration options** – Especially for new team members
✅ **Test configuration changes** – Verify in each environment before release
✅ **Version control karate-config.js** – Track changes to test configuration

