**What Makes WebDriver So Capable:**

**1. Cross-Browser Support**

```java
// Same code works on all browsers
WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
WebDriver driver = new FirefoxDriver();
WebDriver driver = new EdgeDriver();
WebDriver driver = new SafariDriver();
```

| Browser | Driver | Setup |
|---------|--------|-------|
| **Chrome** | ChromeDriver | Download matching version |
| **Firefox** | GeckoDriver | Automatic via WebDriverManager |
| **Edge** | EdgeDriver | Built-in or download |
| **Safari** | SafariDriver | Built-in (macOS only) |

**2. Multiple Locator Strategies**

```java
// Find elements in different ways
driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
driver.findElement(By.name("password"));
driver.findElement(By.className("login-button"));
driver.findElement(By.tagName("button"));
driver.findElement(By.linkText("Click Here"));
driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("Click"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[@id='submit']"));
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#submit"));
```

**3. Advanced Interactions**

```java
// Actions class for complex user interactions
Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

// Mouse actions
actions.moveToElement(element).click().perform();
actions.doubleClick(element).perform();
actions.contextClick(element).perform();
actions.dragAndDrop(source, target).perform();

// Keyboard actions
actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL).sendKeys("a").keyUp(Keys.CONTROL).perform();
```

**4. JavaScript Execution**

```java
// Execute JavaScript directly
JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;
js.executeScript("window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight)");
js.executeScript("arguments[0].click();", element);
js.executeScript("return document.title");
```

**5. Window and Frame Management**

```java
// Switch between windows
