**A Framework for Locator Strategy:**

Choosing the right locator strategy is critical for test reliability and maintainability. This guide provides a systematic approach to selecting and maintaining locators.

**1. Locator Priority Pyramid**

```
        🏆 BEST 🏆
           /\
      data-testid
         /  \
        ID   Name
       /      \
    CSS Selector
     /        \
   XPath     LinkText
    /          \
  PartialText  ClassName
   /            \
 TagName     Absolute XPath
        🚫 WORST 🚫
```

**2. Decision Framework**

```java
public By getBestLocator(WebElement element) {
    // Priority 1: data-testid
    String testId = element.getAttribute("data-testid");
    if (testId != null && !testId.isEmpty()) {
        return By.cssSelector("[data-testid='" + testId + "']");
    }

    // Priority 2: ID
    String id = element.getAttribute("id");
    if (id != null && !id.isEmpty() && !id.matches(".*\\d.*")) { // Avoid numeric IDs
        return By.id(id);
    }

    // Priority 3: Name
    String name = element.getAttribute("name");
    if (name != null && !name.isEmpty()) {
        return By.name(name);
    }

    // Priority 4: Stable CSS combination
    String css = buildStableCssSelector(element);
    if (css != null) {
        return By.cssSelector(css);
    }

    // Priority 5: XPath as last resort
    return By.xpath(buildStableXPath(element));
}

private String buildStableCssSelector(WebElement element) {
    // Build based on stable attributes
    if (element.getAttribute("type") != null) {
        return element.getTagName() + "[type='" + element.getAttribute("type") + "']";
    }
    if (element.getAttribute("placeholder") != null) {
        return element.getTagName() + "[placeholder='" + element.getAttribute("placeholder") + "']";
    }
    return null;
}
```

**3. Stability Checklist**

✅ **Does it have an ID?** – Most stable
✅ **Is it a data attribute?** – Designed for testing
✅ **Is the class name semantic?** – `.btn` may change, `.login-button` less likely
✅ **Does it use position?** – Index-based locators are brittle
✅ **Does it rely on text?** – Text changes frequently
✅ **Is it unique?** – Should find exactly one element

**4. Locator Maintenance Patterns**

**Page Object Model with Locators:**

```java
public class LoginPage {
    // Store locators as constants
    private static final By USERNAME_INPUT = By.cssSelector("[data-testid='username']");
    private static final By PASSWORD_INPUT = By.cssSelector("[data-testid='password']");
    private static final By LOGIN_BUTTON = By.cssSelector("[data-testid='login']");
    private static final By ERROR_MESSAGE = By.cssSelector("[data-testid='error']");

    // Methods use the locators
    public void login(String username, String password) {
        driver.findElement(USERNAME_INPUT).sendKeys(username);
        driver.findElement(PASSWORD_INPUT).sendKeys(password);
        driver.findElement(LOGIN_BUTTON).click();
    }
}
```

