**6. Testing Locator Quality**

```java
// Check uniqueness
public boolean isLocatorUnique(By locator) {
    return driver.findElements(locator).size() == 1;
}

// Check stability (over multiple page loads)
public boolean isLocatorStable(By locator) {
    try {
        driver.navigate().refresh();
        driver.findElement(locator);
        return true;
    } catch (NoSuchElementException e) {
        return false;
    }
}

// Check if locator finds the right element
public boolean isLocatorCorrect(By locator, String expectedText) {
    try {
        WebElement element = driver.findElement(locator);
        return element.getText().contains(expectedText);
    } catch (NoSuchElementException e) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

**7. Common Locator Mistakes**

❌ **Using absolute XPath** – `html/body/div[3]/form/input`
❌ **Relying on index** – `(//div)[3]`
❌ **Using dynamic IDs** – `id="user_12345"`
❌ **Depending on text** – `//*[text()='Submit']` (text changes)
❌ **Too generic** – `//div` or `.item`
❌ **Case sensitivity issues** – `By.linkText("LOGIN")` when text is "Login"
❌ **Not handling visibility** – Finding element before it's visible
❌ **Forgetting frames** – Element exists but in different frame

**8. Locator Strategy Cheat Sheet**

| Situation | Recommended Locator | Example |
|-----------|-------------------|---------|
| **Element has data-testid** | `[data-testid='value']` | `[data-testid='login-button']` |
| **Element has unique ID** | `#id` | `#username` |
| **Form field** | `[name='field']` | `[name='email']` |
| **Button by purpose** | `.btn-primary` or `[data-testid]` | `.btn-primary` |
| **Link by text** | `linkText` or `partialLinkText` | `By.linkText("Sign In")` |
| **Element in list** | Combine parent + child selectors | `#user-list tr:first-child .name` |
| **Dynamic content** | Use waits + stable parent | `#content .dynamic-item` |
| **No good attributes** | XPath with multiple conditions | `//div[contains(@class,'error') and not(contains(@class,'hidden'))]` |

**9. Locator Review Checklist**

✅ **Is it unique?** – finds exactly one element
✅ **Is it readable?** – clear what it finds
✅ **Is it maintainable?** – won't break with minor UI changes
✅ **Is it fast?** – avoids expensive XPath functions
✅ **Is it consistent?** – works across page loads
✅ **Is it independent?** – doesn't rely on element position
✅ **Is it documented?** – why this locator was chosen
✅ **Is it versioned?** – tracks with application changes

